A surface switch sends unsubscribe + subscribe back to back (focus flaps
between the tapped surface and the pane-derived one until pane.list
answers), so the bridge's surface.frames.ended {unsubscribed} for the old
stream routinely lands after the new subscription succeeded. Handling it
dropped the feed the bridge was actually streaming and the card fell back
to polled text — the live screen only showed up on some switches. The
echo carries no information we didn't already act on when sending the
unsubscribe, so it is now ignored; real ends (closed/error/backpressure)
still resubscribe." && git push -q origin feat/responsive-sessions && git log --oneline -1

